name    life
prog    life
# Does it draw, and does the screen change when keys arrive -- AND is the
# status line intact?  That last one is the terminal-size check.  `life' puts
# its status on the bottom row by absolute cursor address, so in a window
# shorter than the 24 lines its termcap promises, the status lands INSIDE the
# board and both are destroyed.  Measured 2026-08-27 at 40x12: the board read
# `Gene@..@@@: 3' where the status crossed it.  This `expect' is what fails
# when that happens; it is the only check here that can see that class of
# bug.
rate    0.7
wait    4
snap    opening
wait    4
snap    played
key     \003
wait    2
expect  Cycles every 8 generations.
